---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import ChoiceListDemo from "../../components/ChoiceListDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Choice List"
  description="Radio or checkbox rows for answering a question, plus a one-line answer summary."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Choice List</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A list of answers to pick from, with an optional typed answer. Use it for
    preference questions and for questions an assistant asks in a chat. When the
    question is done, show the answer with Choice Summary.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ChoiceListDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Choice List usage"
      code={`import { ChoiceList, ChoiceSummary } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/choice-list";

const [style, setStyle] = useState<string[]>([]);

<ChoiceList
  legend="Reply style"
  options={[
    { id: "short", label: "Short answers (Recommended)" },
    { id: "detailed", label: "Detailed answers" },
  ]}
  value={style}
  onChange={setStyle}
/>

<ChoiceList
  layout="compact"
  multiple
  legend="Choose one or more answers"
  options={channels}
  value={choices}
  onChange={setChoices}
  error={attempted && !choices.length ? "Choose an answer." : undefined}
  textOption={{
    id: "custom-answer",
    value: text,
    active: typed,
    onChange: setText,
    onFocus: () => setTyped(true),
    error: null,
  }}
/>

<ChoiceSummary prompt="Reply style" answer="Short answers" />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>value</code> is always an array of option ids, for one answer or many.
      <code>onChange</code> gets the next array, so a state setter can be passed straight
      in.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>layout</code> is <code>"stacked"</code> (bordered 44px rows with radio
      or checkbox marks) or <code>"compact"</code> (36px numbered rows with dividers,
      in a list that scrolls after about six rows). There is no separate size: each
      layout has one row height, and compact rows grow to 44px on touch screens.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>multiple</code> turns radios into checkboxes. In a compact single list
      the legend is for screen readers only, because the question above already names
      it. <code>disabled</code> locks every row, and
      <code>error</code> shows a message under the list and marks each input invalid.
    </p>
    <p>
      An option with <code>recommended</code>, or a label ending in
      <code>(Recommended)</code>, gets a Recommended badge.
      <code>textOption</code> adds a typed answer after the options. A stacked list
      always shows it. A compact list shows it only while
      <code>active</code>, and moves focus into it, so pair it with an "Other
      answer" button whose <code>aria-controls</code> is the
      <code>textOption.id</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ChoiceSummary</code> takes a <code>prompt</code>, an optional
      <code>answer</code> (leave it out for an expired or cancelled question), and
      optional <code>children</code> after the answer.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The list is a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a
      <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code>. Each row is a label around a real radio or
      checkbox input, so Tab, arrow keys, and Space work as they do for native
      controls. A focused row shows a 2px focus ring. Errors are linked with
      <code>aria-describedby</code>, and a typed-answer error is announced.
    </p>
    <p>
      Colors change in 120–180ms, and check marks pop in. Both stop when reduced
      motion is requested. In forced colors mode checked rows and focus use
      system highlight colors.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Rows use <code>--sprout-input</code> borders. Checked rows use
      <code>--sprout-primary-subtle</code> with a <code>--sprout-focus</code>
      border, and check marks use <code>--sprout-primary</code>, so the opt-in
      TulipFarm theme tints them green. Compact numbers sit on
      <code>--sprout-secondary</code>. Errors use <code>--sprout-danger</code>,
      and the summary check uses <code>--sprout-success</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
